  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A mandala that distorts at round 6 cannot be blocked flat at round 10 — consistent gauge from the centre outward is the one structural requirement that determines whether all ten rounds lie flat. This pattern builds a 40 cm mandala in three distinct sections: rounds 1 to 4 establish the flat-circle base using trebles in open spoke groups; rounds 5 to 7 introduce "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shell"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "v-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "V-stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " repeats that open the fabric and add volume; rounds 8 to 10 work "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "double-treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "double treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " arches and a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "picot"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "picot"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " edging. Place a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "stitch-marker"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "stitch marker"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the start of every round and count before joining. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " after round 10 to pull the mandala to full diameter and correct any rippling from the outer rounds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 180 m (200 g). Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, stitch markers (at least 4), blocking mat and pins."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "40 cm diameter in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook after blocking. Gauge matters most on this pattern — check your diameter at the end of round 4 (target: 14 cm). If the circle is smaller, go up half a hook size; if larger, go down."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Double crochet (dc) — UK: short upright stitch"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr) — UK: yarn over once before inserting hook"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Double treble (dtr) — UK: yarn over twice before inserting hook"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "V-stitch: (tr, ch1, tr) into same space"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Shell: 5tr into same space"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Picot: ch3, sl st into first ch"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr throughout). Work 11 tr into the ring. Pull the tail to close the ring. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. (12 tr)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 1 tr in same st. Ch 1. *2 tr in next st, ch 1; repeat from * 10 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. (24 tr, 12 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into ch-1 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr in same ch-1 sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in next ch-1 sp, ch 1; repeat from * 10 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. (36 tr, 12 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into ch-1 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 1 tr in same sp. Ch 2. *(2 tr, ch 2, 2 tr) into next ch-1 sp, ch 2; repeat from * 10 more times. 2 tr in first sp (already started). Ch 2. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. (48 tr, 24 ch-2 sps). Check diameter: 14 cm target."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 5"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into ch-2 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 4 tr in same sp (first shell made). Ch 1. *5 tr in next ch-2 sp, ch 1; repeat from * 22 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. (24 shells of 5 tr, 24 ch-1 sps) = (120 tr, 24 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 6"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into ch-1 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 1 tr, ch 1, 2 tr in same sp (first V-stitch made, with extra width). Work: *(2 tr, ch 1, 2 tr) in next ch-1 sp; repeat from * around. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. (96 tr, 24 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 7"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into ch-1 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work shell of 5 tr in 12 alternate ch-1 sps and V-stitch of (tr, ch 1, tr) in the remaining 12 ch-1 sps, alternating shell and V-stitch throughout. Sl st to top of ch-3 to join. (12 shells + 12 V-stitches) = (72 tr in shells + 24 tr in V-sts, 12 ch-1 sps) = (96 tr, 12 ch-1 sps). Check diameter: 26 cm target."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 8"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to top of first shell's 3rd tr (centre of shell). Ch 4 (counts as first dtr). 1 dtr in same st. Ch 2. *2 dtr into centre tr of next shell or into ch-1 sp of next V-stitch, ch 2; repeat from * 22 more times. Sl st to top of ch-4 to join. (48 dtr, 24 ch-2 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 9"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into ch-2 sp. Ch 4 (counts as first dtr). 2 dtr in same sp. Ch 2. *3 dtr in next ch-2 sp, ch 2; repeat from * 22 more times. Sl st to top of ch-4 to join. (72 dtr, 24 ch-2 sps). Check diameter: 34 cm target."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 10 — picot edging"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 1. 1 dc in first dtr. *Ch 3, sl st into first ch of that ch-3 (picot made). 1 dc in each of next 2 dtr. Into ch-2 sp: 1 dc, picot, 1 dc. 1 dc in each of next 2 dtr. Picot. 1 dc in next dtr; repeat from * around, ending with sl st to first dc. Fasten off. Weave in end. (24 picots along dtr groups, 24 picots in arch spaces) = (48 picots)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 10
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in both ends using a tapestry needle. Soak the mandala in cool water for 10 minutes, squeeze out gently without wringing, and roll in a towel to remove excess moisture. Pin to a blocking mat at 40 cm diameter, placing pins every 2 cm around the outer picot edge. Leave until fully dry (at least 24 hours for DK cotton). The mandala will not lie flat without blocking at this diameter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As a standalone piece the mandala does not need joining. To use as a shawl centrepiece, join to surrounding motifs by replacing picots on the final round with slip-stitch joins into corresponding points on adjacent motifs. Work the joining picots as: ch 1, sl st into corresponding picot on adjacent motif, ch 1, sl st back into the current stitch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 degrees on a gentle cycle. Reshape while damp and dry flat. Do not tumble dry. Re-block if the mandala loses shape after washing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Once the ten-round mandala sits flat, try working the same construction in two colours — change after round 4 for a two-tone result, or change at every even round for a striped effect. The flat-circle base (rounds 1 to 4) also serves as the start of a round cushion cover: continue past round 10 until the circle reaches 22 cm diameter for the front panel."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}